1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,980
On 13 September 1993, on
the lawn of the White House,

2
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:17,580
the prime minister of Israel
shook hands with Yasser Arafat,

3
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,360
the leader of the Palestine
Liberation Organization.

4
00:00:21,126 --> 00:00:24,686
He was Yitzhak Rabin, and he had
spent his whole life as a soldier.

5
00:00:36,395 --> 00:00:40,640
He was the army's chief of staff when
Israel won the Six-Day War in 1967.

6
00:00:41,494 --> 00:00:44,894
Then, as defence minister during
the first Palestinian uprising,

7
00:00:45,654 --> 00:00:47,814
he ordered the army to
put it down by force.

8
00:00:48,394 --> 00:00:50,594
As prime minister, he chose to negotiate.

9
00:01:01,767 --> 00:01:03,927
His government made a
deal with his old enemy.

10
00:01:04,807 --> 00:01:09,587
Israel would pull back from Gaza and Jericho,
and Palestinians would govern themselves there.

11
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:20,940
The talks that led to it had
been held in secret in Norway,

12
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:23,440
which gave the Oslo agreement its name.

13
00:01:29,562 --> 00:01:32,687
In October 1994 he signed
a peace treaty with Jordan,

14
00:01:33,067 --> 00:01:37,307
and that December he shared the Nobel
Peace Prize with Arafat and Shimon Peres.

15
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:40,220
But many Israelis opposed all of it.

16
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:43,660
Some believed that the whole West
Bank belonged to the Jewish people,

17
00:01:43,1000 --> 00:01:45,660
and that Rabin was giving it away.

18
00:01:46,252 --> 00:01:49,017
Through 1995 the protests grew angrier.

19
00:01:49,877 --> 00:01:54,537
Posters showed Rabin in an SS uniform, and
crowds called him a traitor and a murderer.

20
00:01:55,195 --> 00:01:59,895
A few rabbis argued that under Jewish law,
a leader who gave up land could be treated

21
00:01:59,895 --> 00:02:02,175
as a rodef, a pursuer, and killed.

22
00:02:02,692 --> 00:02:05,657
The Shin Bet, Israel's
internal security service,

23
00:02:05,977 --> 00:02:10,977
had warned since 1993 that a Jewish
extremist might try to assassinate him.

24
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:16,815
And on Saturday, 4 November, supporters of
the peace process called a rally in Tel Aviv.

25
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:26,300
The rally was held in Kings of Israel
Square, in front of Tel Aviv city hall,

26
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:28,400
and more than one hundred
thousand people came.

27
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:32,745
There were banners, speeches
and songs, and in the footage,

28
00:02:33,065 --> 00:02:33,745
Rabin is smiling.

29
00:02:34,462 --> 00:02:37,702
He told the crowd that he had always
believed most people want peace,

30
00:02:38,122 --> 00:02:39,802
and are ready to take a risk for it.

31
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:44,129
At the end, the singer Miri Aloni
led everyone in the Song for Peace,

32
00:02:44,489 --> 00:02:46,249
and Rabin and Peres sang along.

33
00:02:46,813 --> 00:02:50,273
Rabin folded the page with the words
and put it in his jacket pocket.

34
00:02:50,859 --> 00:02:53,259
He walked down the steps of
city hall toward his car.

35
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:58,839
Waiting in the parking area was Yigal Amir, a
twenty-five-year-old law student from Herzliya.

36
00:02:59,342 --> 00:03:03,082
He had been there for some time, and
no security officer had questioned him.

37
00:03:03,626 --> 00:03:07,451
As Rabin reached the car, Amir stepped
through what looked like a gap in the security

38
00:03:07,451 --> 00:03:09,091
cordon, and fired three shots.

39
00:03:09,769 --> 00:03:13,069
Two hit Rabin. The third
wounded his bodyguard,

40
00:03:13,409 --> 00:03:16,569
Yoram Rubin. Security men
seized Amir on the spot.

41
00:03:17,074 --> 00:03:20,419
Rabin was rushed to Ichilov
Hospital, where he died that night.

42
00:03:20,699 --> 00:03:22,119
He was seventy-three years old.

43
00:03:22,652 --> 00:03:26,372
His aide Eitan Haber announced
the death shortly after eleven.

44
00:03:39,228 --> 00:03:41,973
On Sunday, his coffin lay
in state at the Knesset,

45
00:03:42,273 --> 00:03:45,113
and about a million people,
according to reports at the time,

46
00:03:45,393 --> 00:03:46,173
filed past it.

47
00:03:46,623 --> 00:03:50,583
On Monday, 6 November, he was
buried on Mount Herzl in Jerusalem.

48
00:03:51,483 --> 00:03:55,743
Delegations came from about eighty
countries, among them sixty heads of state.

49
00:03:56,250 --> 00:04:00,695
Egypt's president, Hosni Mubarak,
visited Jerusalem for the first time,

50
00:04:00,915 --> 00:04:03,795
and Jordan's King Hussein
came as Israel's guest.

51
00:04:04,575 --> 00:04:07,435
Arafat stayed away, reportedly
because of security fears.

52
00:04:08,044 --> 00:04:11,764
King Hussein, whose army
had fought Israel in 1967,

53
00:04:12,424 --> 00:04:14,604
spoke of Rabin as a brother and a friend.

54
00:04:26,372 --> 00:04:29,247
President Clinton recalled the
ceremony on the White House lawn,

55
00:04:29,647 --> 00:04:32,527
and the stage Rabin had
asked the world to look at.

56
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,480
Then he spoke about the murder itself.

57
00:04:55,562 --> 00:04:58,287
Rabin's granddaughter, Noa
Ben-Artzi, was seventeen.

58
00:04:58,967 --> 00:05:00,527
She called him her personal hero.

59
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:15,760
Then Eitan Haber, who had
written many of Rabin's speeches,

60
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,580
held up the page from the rally.

61
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,700
He said that the blood on
it was between the lines,

62
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:21,680
between the words.

63
00:05:36,328 --> 00:05:37,893
President Clinton ended in Hebrew.

64
00:05:52,462 --> 00:05:54,947
Amir was arrested at the
scene, with his pistol,

65
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:58,147
and he confessed. He said
that he had acted for God.

66
00:05:58,745 --> 00:06:02,010
On the day of the funeral, a court
held a custody hearing for him.

67
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:15,920
His trial opened in Tel Aviv in
January 1996, before three judges.

68
00:06:16,662 --> 00:06:20,982
On 27 March they convicted him of
murder and of wounding the bodyguard,

69
00:06:21,502 --> 00:06:24,502
and sentenced him to life
in prison, plus six years.

70
00:06:25,190 --> 00:06:30,115
The presiding judge, Edmond Levy, said Amir
had acted with premeditation and amazing

71
00:06:30,115 --> 00:06:33,915
calm, and he rejected the claim that
Jewish law justified the killing.

72
00:06:34,561 --> 00:06:36,401
Amir called the trial a show trial.

73
00:06:37,001 --> 00:06:40,101
In August 1996 the Supreme
Court rejected his appeal.

74
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:43,961
His brother Hagai and Dror Adani
were later convicted of conspiracy.

75
00:06:52,733 --> 00:06:57,893
The day after the verdict, on 28 March, the
Shamgar Commission published its report.

76
00:06:58,653 --> 00:07:00,733
It had been appointed four
days after the murder,

77
00:07:01,253 --> 00:07:02,913
and it had heard seventy-two witnesses.

78
00:07:03,705 --> 00:07:06,790
It found that the Shin Bet
had failed in its main task,

79
00:07:07,150 --> 00:07:08,930
which was to protect the prime minister.

80
00:07:09,464 --> 00:07:12,829
Warnings about a Jewish assassin
had not become real protection.

81
00:07:13,489 --> 00:07:16,429
The police and the Shin Bet had
not coordinated their plans,

82
00:07:16,709 --> 00:07:19,729
and nobody had properly checked
the parking area where Amir waited.

83
00:07:20,384 --> 00:07:24,189
It held the Shin Bet chief, Carmi
Gillon, who had already resigned,

84
00:07:24,489 --> 00:07:29,029
directly responsible, and it recommended
removing the head of the VIP protection unit

85
00:07:29,029 --> 00:07:31,209
and censuring the Tel
Aviv police commander.

86
00:07:41,162 --> 00:07:45,247
The commission also said there was no basis
for the conspiracy claims about a second

87
00:07:45,247 --> 00:07:49,927
gunman. The Supreme Court judges called
such claims fictional detective stories.

88
00:07:50,621 --> 00:07:53,546
What the commission did not
examine was the wider climate.

89
00:07:54,266 --> 00:07:56,666
Its task was the security
of the prime minister,

90
00:07:57,026 --> 00:07:58,326
not the culture of the protests.

91
00:07:59,116 --> 00:08:04,841
In 2001 the Knesset barred parole boards from
recommending any pardon or shorter sentence

92
00:08:04,841 --> 00:08:06,841
for the murderer of a prime minister.

93
00:08:07,495 --> 00:08:12,715
Kings of Israel Square is now Rabin Square,
and every year Israel holds a memorial day

94
00:08:12,715 --> 00:08:14,655
for him, on the Hebrew date of his death.

95
00:08:15,878 --> 00:08:17,543
The record is clear about that night.

96
00:08:17,923 --> 00:08:19,823
What does it tell you
about the days before it?
